projects:
- name: Market Geometry - Time-Resolved Density Estimation on Transaction Data
  type: Independent quantitative research
  stack: Python, PyTorch/CUDA, pandas, NumPy, statsmodels, Shapely
  facts:
  - Built a GPU-accelerated kernel density estimator over 242,605 NYC property transactions
    from 2015-2024 to measure how local price structure varies across market segments
    and changes over time.
  - Derived analytic gradients and adapted bandwidth to local sample density.
  - Implemented a strictly causal temporal weighting system with zero lookahead and
    a walk-forward validation harness across 72 time slices on a 400x400 state-space
    grid.
  - Built the analysis around point-in-time correctness so future observations could
    not contaminate historical estimates.
  - Derived analytic gradients, time derivatives, and field-calculus diagnostics including
    flux, divergence, and continuity residuals to localize where transaction activity
    accumulates or dissipates.
  - Used GPU-based numerical computation to make large-scale, time-resolved estimation
    practical.
